% \subsection{Data}
%
% To compose several parts of the thesis layout, input from the thesis author is required.
% For the |istaustriathesis| class, this is realized by the commands provided in Section~\ref{sec:user:data}.
% Additional data can be defined with the the commands in the remainder of this section.
%
% \DescribeMacro{\CreateData}
% Used as |\CreateData|\marg{name}, it generates a command |\set|\meta{name}.
% Used as |\set|\meta{name}\marg{string}, the newly created command assigns the value \meta{string} to the internal variable |\istaustriathesis@data@|\meta{name}.
% The variable is initialized with an error value to alert the user of the fact that \meta{string} was not supplied via the |\set|\meta{name} command.
% Furthermore, a command |\istaustriathesis@data@|\meta{name}|@def| is created, to increase source code readability when verifying the existence of a specific data item.
% See Section~\ref{sec:impl:data:declarations} for examples.
%
% \DescribeMacro{\CreatePerson}
% Used as |\CreatePerson|\marg{name}, it generates a command |\set|\meta{name}.
% Used as |\set|\meta{name}\marg{pretitle}\marg{personname}\marg{posttitle}\marg{affiliation}, the newly created command assigns the supplied values to the corresponding internal variables |\istaustriathesis@person@|\meta{name}|@|\textellipsis as given in the table below.
% \begin{center}
% \begin{tabular}{lllc}
%   \toprule
%   Argument & Internal Variable\\
%   \midrule
%                      & |\istaustriathesis@person@|\meta{name}|@def|         \\
%   \meta{pretitle}    & |\istaustriathesis@person@|\meta{name}|@pretitle|    \\
%   \meta{personname}  & |\istaustriathesis@person@|\meta{name}|@name|        \\
%   \meta{posttitle}   & |\istaustriathesis@person@|\meta{name}|@posttitle|   \\
%   \meta{affiliation} & |\istaustriathesis@person@|\meta{name}|@affiliation| \\
%   \bottomrule
% \end{tabular}
% \end{center}
% The command |\istaustriathesis@person@|\meta{name}|@def| is created to increase source code readability when verifying the existence of a specific person.
% Furthermore, the command |\istaustriathesis@person@|\meta{name}|@name| returns the person's name.
% The name can be extended by the person's titles using |\istaustriathesis@person@|\meta{name}|@fullname| and -- even further -- with the person's affilition using |\textellipsis|\meta{name}|@fullnameaffiliation|.
% See Section~\ref{sec:impl:data:declarations} for examples.
%
